hey everyone i'm john coogan and here's  why you should spend your valuable time  listening to me  talk about startups first i'm an  entrepreneur myself  i've been working on my own startup  since 2012 and i've seen a lot of  different perspectives that i think are  important to share  i've been a co-founder of three  companies i've been a ceo  a cto and a cmo i've served on multiple  boards and have even been an investor  this variety of experience is important  because companies are defined by their  management team  their board of directors and their  shareholders the incentives between  these groups are not always perfectly  aligned  and it's important to understand how  they can diverge if you really want to  know how startups work  i also have experience with companies at  a variety of stages  while my first company only raised  seventeen thousand dollars before  failing a mere five months after  incorporation  my second company soylent raised over 80  million dollars and has been making  money for over seven years now  the decisions faced by a two-person team  going through an incubator  are usually pretty different from those  faced by a series b company expanding  into new markets  my goal is to bring this experience to  bear when analyzing prominent business  case studies  as well as the more fundamental  questions being debated in the startup  community  lastly and more importantly than any  credential or resume bullet  is the fact that i constantly strive to  maintain a balanced view of the world  i love testing counterfactuals and  playing devil's advocate  i never turn down the opportunity to  listen to someone with who i disagree  and i'm always willing to reevaluate a  deeply held position  from first principles i take a very  deliberate approach with my media diet  always trying to find perspectives that  i'm not hearing from and fill them in  there are always two sides to every  story sometimes those sides are equally  reasonable  and sometimes one side is completely  insane but it's still important in my  opinion to understand the other side  my hope is that you will find my  opinions to be well researched  and as objective as possible my goal  with this channel is a little different  than other youtube channels  i'm not trying to grow a large audience  or monetize with ads or sponsorships  i want this channel to be my calling  card in the business world and give you  insight into how i think  the decision to partner with someone in  a business context shouldn't be taken  lightly  often you only have a few hours of real  face-to-face interaction with someone  before deciding to sign documents that  could link you for years  i want anyone who plans on doing  business with me to be able to spend as  much time as they want diligencing my  thought process  since my thought process is ultimately  what you get when you work with me  i also want to connect with the next  generation of entrepreneurs who may be  searching youtube for ways to solve a  hard problem that they're facing  i want to be able to find and invest in  the best startups out there and the next  generation of great entrepreneurs  are watching youtube right now so if  you're building something cool  please reach out to me i really hope you  enjoy my content and consider  subscribing to the channel to get  updates i try and post new videos weekly  and i'm always reading the comments  thanks for watching this video and  subscribing to the channel
 

